eally uneasy she's  kind of like scared to go outside and at  one point she even like snaps at jane  which she's never done before and every  now and then like one of the group will  kind of see like a shadow moving around  like behind the trees or just outside  the windows that looks too big to be an  elk or a wolf then a bit later on uh the  gang find this big smear of what appears  to be blood in the snow not too far from  the cabin now they don't see a body like  you know not a human body or an animal  body or anything so they assume oh maybe  it was just roadkill or it was a  predator that dragged off a deer or  something like that  uh but even more ominously april who  actually when they went snowboarding she  was like [ __ ] this [ __ ] and like stayed  in the lodge uh she overheard like a  couple of guys talking about us you know  talking about like the search and rescue  who had found a dead guy up there like  last season so all these little things  are going on and meanwhile we as the  reader uh know that the monsters are out  there because every now and then we  witness some hapless skiers or some tow  truck drivers or something like that get  eviscerated by these same monsters now  the origins of the monsters themselves  are never really explained all that  heavily which i think was probably a  good idea  but they don't appear to be supernatural  in any way i guess they kind of have  maybe a slight resemblance to a wendigo  but it's not really there's no like  mythology or folklore or anything like  that about them um because like i said  it's kind of like from these people's  point of view and they don't know what  the animals are um the animals are kind  of like described they're very very tall  and they're very very thin like  emaciated looking they have really long  spindly limbs they can climb they can  run they're really fast they have like  really really big huge teeth like these  creepy like black eyes and they're  really really super strong and 